% -------------------- 5. TESTING AND QUALITY --------------------
\chapter{Testing Strategy and Quality Assurance}

Railway-Madad Version 2.0 follows an isolated backend testing architecture designed for deterministic execution and CI/CD scalability. The test strategy combines route-level API contract validation and controller-level business-rule validation. Authentication middleware is mock-driven and supports explicit state simulation (valid, missing, malformed, expired, forbidden), allowing comprehensive negative-path verification without integration coupling.

\section{Test Architecture}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{>{\bfseries}p{0.26\textwidth}Y}
\toprule
\rowcolor{TableHeader}
\textcolor{TableHeaderText}{Layer} & \textcolor{TableHeaderText}{Implementation} \\
\midrule
Test Runner & Jest with project-specific config under unit-test workspace. \\
API Invocation & Supertest against in-memory Express app (no production server startup). \\
Isolation & No real DB/network dependencies; controller and middleware behavior mocked as required. \\
Auth Simulation & Explicit state toggles: valid, missing, malformed, expired, forbidden. \\
Route Contract Scope & Modular route suites covering user/admin/staff/complaint/catering/emergency/food/news/feedback/lost\&found/superadmin/system flows. \\
Controller Unit Scope & Focused unit suites for user, complaint, catering, emergency, and lost\&found logic. \\
Error Contract Coverage & Assertions include 400/401/403/404/500 negative path checks. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

